Fact-DB

A database of facts that keeps every version.

Fact::DB holds facts about entities in memory. Every transaction makes a
new database value and leaves the old one as it was, so any version can be
read and queried. Queries are written in Datalog, with rules.

Requires a C compiler, perl 5.10 or later, and HAMT.


INSTALLATION

To install this module, run the following commands:

	perl Makefile.PL
	make
	make test
	make install

SUPPORT AND DOCUMENTATION

After installing, you can find documentation for this module with the
perldoc command.

    perldoc Fact::DB

You can also look for information at:

    RT, CPAN's request tracker (report bugs here)
        https://rt.cpan.org/NoAuth/Bugs.html?Dist=Fact-DB

    Search CPAN
        https://metacpan.org/release/Fact-DB


